// Biome lints and formats the TypeScript, JavaScript, Svelte, Astro, JSON and
// CSS. mise.toml pins it; CI's lint job runs `biome ci`, and `bun run lint` /
// `bun run format` run it locally.
{
  "$schema": "https://biomejs.dev/schemas/2.5.15/schema.json",
  // .gitignore decides what is skipped: node_modules, build output, the docs
  // site's generated.json.
  "vcs": { "enabled": true, "clientKind": "git", "useIgnoreFile": true, "defaultBranch": "main" },
  // The tray's packages.lock.json files are NuGet's output, written without a
  // final newline (Renovate's too), so Biome and editorconfig-checker
  // (.editorconfig-checker.json) leave them as NuGet wrote them.
  "files": { "ignoreUnknown": true, "includes": ["**", "!**/packages.lock.json"] },
  "formatter": { "indentStyle": "space", "indentWidth": 2, "lineWidth": 120, "lineEnding": "lf" },
  "javascript": { "formatter": { "quoteStyle": "single", "trailingCommas": "all", "arrowParentheses": "always" } },
  "css": { "formatter": { "quoteStyle": "single" } },
  // Parses and formats the markup of .svelte, .astro and .html files too, not
  // just their scripts, so a name used only in the markup does not show up as
  // unused. Script and style blocks stay indented and void elements keep their
  // `/>`, as Svelte's own formatting has them.
  "html": {
    "experimentalFullSupportEnabled": true,
    "formatter": { "enabled": true, "indentScriptAndStyle": true, "selfCloseVoidElements": "always" }
  },
  "linter": {
    "enabled": true,
    "rules": {
      "preset": "recommended",
      // The rules below start as warnings; each is fixed across the code and
      // then raised to an error in its own PR.
      "suspicious": { "noConsole": "warn", "noExplicitAny": "warn" },
      "style": { "noNonNullAssertion": "warn" },
      // `(a(), b())` in arrow bodies is deliberate here: it keeps one-line
      // callbacks one line.
      "complexity": { "noCommaOperator": "off" },
      // Type-aware rules: they turn on Biome's type inference.
      "nursery": { "noFloatingPromises": "warn", "noMisusedPromises": "warn", "useExhaustiveSwitchCases": "warn" }
    }
  },
  "assist": { "enabled": true, "actions": { "source": { "organizeImports": "on" } } },
  "overrides": [
    {
      // Build and dev scripts and the e2e tests talk to whoever runs them.
      "includes": ["scripts/**", "docs/scripts/**", "e2e/**"],
      "linter": { "rules": { "suspicious": { "noConsole": "off" } } }
    },
    {
      // noUncheckedIndexedAccess makes `!` the plain way for a test to say
      // "this element exists"; a wrong guess fails the test anyway.
      "includes": ["**/test/**", "**/*.test.ts", "**/*.test.tsx", "e2e/**"],
      "linter": { "rules": { "style": { "noNonNullAssertion": "off" } } }
    }
  ]
}
